# .markdownlintignore — markdownlint's committed exclusion list (gitignore
# syntax). markdownlint-cli auto-detects this file; paths listed here are not
# linted and not rewritten by `--fix`.
#
# This file exists instead of `--ignore` flags on the command line. A
# markdownlint-cli `--ignore` argument is `lstat`ed: a real directory expands
# to its whole subtree, but a glob string throws, falls to the catch branch,
# and becomes a pattern matched against `.md` file paths. No `.md` path ends
# in `node_modules`, so `--ignore '**/node_modules'` matched nothing at all,
# and `--ignore book` worked only because `book/` happened to exist as a real
# directory at lint time. Keeping the list here also keeps the `fmt` and
# `check` recipes from drifting apart, and mirrors the `.primignore`
# convention.

# Vendored dependencies — the VS Code extension's, and any other.
node_modules/

# mdBook build output.
book/

# Cargo build output — `cargo doc` writes Markdown there.
target/
